<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Rajkot State</h1><p class="st-meta">1620 CE – 1948 CE · capital Rajkot</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Jadeja Rajput state of Kathiawar whose capital hosted the British agency for the peninsula and where Gandhi spent his boyhood.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Rajkot was founded in 1620 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vibhaji-ajoji">Vibhaji Ajoji</a>, a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jam-sataji">Jam Sataji of Nawanagar</a>, who received the area as his share. The town was later briefly held by Mughal officers, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jadeja">Jadeja</a> line recovered it.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Thakore Sahibs ruled a small territory, but Rajkot became important as the seat of the British agency for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Kathiawar</a> and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajkumar-college-rajkot">Rajkumar College</a> for princes. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karamchand-gandhi">Karamchand Gandhi</a>, father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Mohandas Gandhi</a>, served as its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diwan">diwan</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lakhajirajsinhji-ii">Lakhajirajsinhji II</a> introduced a representative assembly, while the 1939 Rajkot satyagraha challenged his successor.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Rajkot merged into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saurashtra-state">United State of Saurashtra</a> in 1948 and served as that state's capital until 1956. It became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bombay-state">Bombay State</a> and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> in 1960, and is now one of Gujarat's largest cities.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/rajkot-state.jpg" alt="Rajkot State" width="320" height="192"><figcaption>Image: Roberto Breschi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Rajkot_Principality.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1620 CE – 1948 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>